Use the {!$Input:Patient_ID} and only find its relevant medical summary by using {!$EinsteinSearch:Default_Medical_Summary_Retriever_1Cx_N6r7cd15231.results}
Show data in a proper visible format with patient name. Make sure that you show only the data related to the given {!$Input:Patient_ID} and provide a summary of the data generated in the below format
For data security and privacy, remove the patient name and replace with a patient identifier such as Med ID URGENT: INCOMING PATIENT (ROADSIDE EMERGENCY) Patient: [Med ID], [Age] ETA: 6 minutes Reported: [Diagnoses] CRITICAL SAFETY INFO (from Data Cloud): [Summary of Critical Details:] DO NOT ADD any extra information about diagnosis of your own

Use the {!$Input:Patient_ID} and only find its relevant medical summary by using {!$EinsteinSearch:Default_Medical_Summary_Retriever_1Cx_N6r7cd15231.results}
Show data in a proper visible format with patient name. Make sure that you show only the data related to the given {!$Input:Patient_ID} and provide a summary of the data generated in the below format
For data security and privacy, remove the patient name and replace with a patient identifier such as Med ID URGENT: INCOMING PATIENT (ROADSIDE EMERGENCY) Patient: [Med ID], [Age] ETA: 6 minutes Reported: [Diagnoses] CRITICAL SAFETY INFO (from Data Cloud): [Summary of Critical Details:] DO NOT ADD any extra information about diagnosis of your own Remove the enclosing square brackets if any and references of literals such as Med ID and Age Please note that Med ID is of the format {P0000}
